# Force LF everywhere, on every platform, for every checkout — the root
# cause of the manifest.json mismatch between a Windows working tree
# (core.autocrlf=true converts stored LF to CRLF on checkout) and CI's
# Linux runner (checks out exactly what's stored, LF). Without this, the
# same commit produces two different sets of file hashes depending on which
# OS generated manifest.json, which defeats the point of a checksum-based
# evidence file. `text=auto` still lets git skip binaries by content
# detection; `eol=lf` pins the normalized line ending instead of leaving it
# to each platform's core.autocrlf default.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything under a build-output directory is binary/generated regardless of
# extension — don't let text=auto's content sniffing guess wrong on these.
07_PLATFORM/dotnet-client/**/bin/** -text
07_PLATFORM/dotnet-client/**/obj/** -text
